## Deployment Description (Methods Section)

> **Mathematical Guarantees of the Autonomous Continuous-Flow Denoising Block.**
> Each denoising block $T_\tau: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^2$ evaluates the exact time-$\tau$ flow map $T_\tau(z) := \Phi_\tau(z)$ ($\tau > 0$) of the autonomous gradient system $\dot{z} = -\nabla f(z)$ governed by the smooth, $1$-strongly convex Lyapunov energy $f(x,y) = \frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 2y^2) + \frac{1}{4}(x+y)^4$ ($\nabla^2 f(z) \succeq I_2$), whose unique global minimizer and equilibrium is the origin $z^* = (0,0)$. The forward flow is globally well-posed on $[0, \infty)$ and guarantees both strict Euclidean contraction and exponential energy dissipation across every single block:
> $$\|T_\tau(z) - T_\tau(w)\| \le e^{-\tau}\|z - w\| \qquad \text{and} \qquad f(T_\tau(z)) \le e^{-2\tau} f(z) \qquad \forall z, w \in \mathbb{R}^2.$$
> Because $T_\tau = \Phi_\tau$ is an exact autonomous flow rather than a discrete time-stepping scheme, stacking $n$ identical blocks $Z_n = T_\tau^n(Z_0)$ obeys exact semigroup additivity $T_\tau^n = \Phi_{n\tau}$, guaranteeing global geometric perturbation stability $\|T_\tau^n(Z_0) - T_\tau^n(W_0)\| \le e^{-n\tau}\|Z_0 - W_0\|$, exponential state convergence $\|Z_n\| \le e^{-n\tau}\|Z_0\|$ to $z^* = (0,0)$, and exponential energy decay $f(Z_n) \le e^{-2n\tau} f(Z_0)$ governed solely by the cumulative integration horizon $n\tau$.
>
> **Distinction Between Flow Horizon $\tau$ and Proximal Regularization.**
> In our proximal notation $\operatorname{prox}_r(z) = \operatorname{argmin}_u \{r(u) + \frac{1}{2}\|u - z\|^2\}$, the quadratic fidelity term carries a fixed unit coefficient $\frac{1}{2}$; an implicit-Euler discretization of $\dot{z} = -\nabla f(z)$ with step size $\tau$ would therefore take the proximal form $J_\tau(z) = (I + \tau \nabla f)^{-1}(z) = \operatorname{prox}_{\tau f}(z) = \operatorname{argmin}_u \{\tau f(u) + \frac{1}{2}\|u - z\|^2\}$, where $\tau$ acts as a scalar multiplier on the regularizer $f$ (and $J_\tau^n \neq J_{n\tau}$). By contrast, in our deployed block $T_\tau = \Phi_\tau$, $\tau > 0$ is the continuous ODE integration time. Furthermore, although $T_\tau$ agrees with $\operatorname{prox}_{\tau f}$ to first order as $\tau \downarrow 0$ ($\Phi_\tau(z) = \operatorname{prox}_{\tau f}(z) + O(\tau^2)$) and is a strict $e^{-\tau}$-contraction, the non-commutativity of the quadratic and quartic Hessians of $f$ renders the flow Jacobian $D\Phi_\tau(z)$ asymmetric ($\operatorname{curl}\Phi_\tau \not\equiv 0$) and causes $\Phi_\tau$ to violate firm nonexpansiveness at large amplitudes for every $\tau > 0$. Consequently, the exact block $T_\tau = \Phi_\tau$ is **not** a proximal map $\operatorname{prox}_{r_\tau}$ for any proper, lower-semicontinuous convex function $r_\tau$; its regularization and stability guarantees are instead rigorously certified by its exact $e^{-\tau}$-Lipschitz contractivity and $e^{-2\tau}$-Lyapunov energy dissipation.
